      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "A susceptibility of a paramagnetic material at $27^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ is $\\chi$. At what temperature will its susceptibility become $\\frac{\\chi}{3}$?",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$627^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$900^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$300^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$81^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "According to Curie's Law, susceptibility $\\chi \\propto \\frac{1}{T}$ where $T$ is absolute temperature.\n$T_1 = 27^\\circ\\mathrm{C} = 300\\ \\mathrm{K}$.\n$\\chi_2 = \\frac{\\chi_1}{3} \\implies T_2 = 3T_1 = 3 \\times 300\\ \\mathrm{K} = 900\\ \\mathrm{K}$.\nIn Celsius, $T_2 = 900 - 273 = 627^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$."
    },
